---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Unit from '../components/Unit.astro';
import { unitByMidi } from '../data/site';

const unit = unitByMidi.get(67)!;
// lib/data/settings_repository.dart, in beats.
const tolerances = [
  { name: 'Relaxed', perfect: 0.15, good: 0.3, okay: 0.45, miss: 0.7 },
  { name: 'Normal', perfect: 0.1, good: 0.2, okay: 0.3, miss: 0.5 },
  { name: 'Strict', perfect: 0.06, good: 0.12, okay: 0.2, miss: 0.35 },
];
const beatMs = 60000 / 80;
---
<Base title="Early, late, on the beat" description={unit.description} note={unit.midi}>
  <Unit unit={unit}>
    <p class="lede" slot="lede" data-split="lines" data-intro data-delay="0.15">
      Every note has a window around its beat. Where you land inside it decides the grade.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        At the normal tolerance, a note within a tenth of a beat is perfect, within two tenths is good and
        within three tenths is okay. Half a beat late, it counts as missed. Stage one runs at 80 beats a
        minute, so one beat lasts {beatMs} milliseconds and perfect means within {beatMs * 0.1}.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="figure figure--windows" data-tap>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 170" role="img" aria-labelledby="windows-title" focusable="false">
        <title id="windows-title">Timing windows around a beat at 80 beats a minute, from 225 milliseconds early to 375 late</title>
        <rect class="band band--okay" x="200" y="70" width="240" height="60" />
        <rect class="band band--good" x="240" y="77" width="160" height="46" />
        <rect class="band band--perfect" x="280" y="84" width="80" height="32" />
        <line class="fig-rule" x1="20" y1="100" x2="620" y2="100" />
        <line class="fig-beat" x1="320" y1="70" x2="320" y2="144" />
        <line class="fig-miss" x1="520" y1="70" x2="520" y2="144" />
        <g class="fig-beat-head" data-tap-head transform="translate(320 30)">
          <ellipse rx="10.4" ry="8" transform="rotate(-20.05)" />
        </g>
        <g data-tap-marks></g>
        <g class="fig-label" text-anchor="middle">
          <text x="320" y="62">perfect</text><text class="tick--minor" x="380" y="62">good</text><text class="tick--minor" x="420" y="62">okay</text>
          <text x="520" y="62">missed</text>
          <text x="200" y="160">-225</text><text class="tick--minor" x="240" y="160">-150</text><text class="tick--minor" x="280" y="160">-75</text>
          <text x="320" y="160">0 ms</text><text class="tick--minor" x="360" y="160">+75</text><text class="tick--minor" x="400" y="160">+150</text>
          <text x="440" y="160">+225</text><text x="520" y="160">+375</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <figcaption>
        <span>Try it at 80 beats a minute. Start, then tap on each beat.</span>
        <span class="tap">
          <button class="toggle toggle--inline" type="button" aria-pressed="false" data-tap-start>Start the beat</button>
          <button class="tap__pad" type="button" data-tap-pad disabled>Tap</button>
          <span class="tap__out" data-tap-out aria-live="polite"></span>
        </span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="table">
      <caption>Tolerance settings, in beats</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Setting</th><th scope="col">Perfect</th><th scope="col">Good</th><th scope="col">Okay</th><th scope="col">Missed after</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {tolerances.map((t) => (
          <tr><th scope="row">{t.name}</th><td>±{t.perfect}</td><td>±{t.good}</td><td>±{t.okay}</td><td>+{t.miss}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Relaxed widens every window for beginners; strict narrows perfect to six hundredths of a beat. The
        speed control slows the whole level down, and the windows stretch with it, because they are counted
        in beats, not milliseconds.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Unit>
</Base>
